; The departure, whole. Local metres, and placed in a level by copying the intro's own
; transform -- the two shots are composed against the same car in the same bore.
;
; POSES ARE IN THIS SCENE'S SPACE, NOT THE LEVEL'S, which is why AnimationPlayer.root_node
; points three levels up at this root rather than at the level. It carries its own car and
; shaft for that reason and no other: a track path that walked out into the level would
; resolve against nodes that are not there while you are authoring it.
;
; NO WorldEnvironment and NO Miners. PlayerView writes fog into the level's shared
; environment, and a second one here would repaint the level; and the crew going home is
; the player, not a set of stand-ins.

[gd_scene load_steps=11 format=3]

